The plan of this section:
2.2.1 a line and the coordinate axes (where a line cuts the \(x\)-axis and the \(y\)-axis);
2.2.2 two lines (at most one meeting point);
2.2.3 a line and a parabola (two, one or no meeting points).
In every case the same idea works: a point on both graphs has the same \(x\) and the same \(y\) on both.
